l it stops absorbing (a flood-coat technique), wiping away excess before it dries on the surface, which uses more product per square foot than a simple roll-on acrylic and contributes to a higher effective cost. Coverage varies widely by stone porosity, from 100-300 square feet per gallon, and pricing runs $80-100+ per gallon, but the 7-15 year service life on well-prepared stone makes the cost-per-year very competitive despite the higher sticker price.",
