          <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-2xl p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-sm font-black text-amber-800 mb-2">Our Recommended Combination Approach</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-amber-700">
              For a concrete paver patio where sand washout has already become a problem, apply <strong>Techniseal Perma Sealer</strong> to the joints first for deep sand stabilization, then follow with a light topcoat of <strong>Foundation Armor AR350</strong> across the full surface once the joint product has fully cured, for both maximum sand retention and a rich wet-look finish. For natural stone hardscapes, skip the film-forming products entirely and use <strong>DryTreat Stain-Proof Original</strong> alone, pairing it with a separate joint sand stabilizer product if sand retention on the stone's joints is also a concern.
            </p>
